.SH "نام (NAME)"
lr_rawmail2mail \- deanonymizes and formats a report from an email message
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBlr_rawmail2mail\fR \fB[\fR\f(BIoptions\fR\fB]\fR \fIdumpstem\fR \fIaddresses\fR...
.PP
\&\fBlr_rawmail2mail\fR \fB\-h\fR
.PP
\&\fBlr_rawmail2mail\fR \fB\-v\fR
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
.IP \fB\-h\fR 4
.IX Item "-h"
Prints usage information and exits.
.IP \fB\-i\fR 4
.IX Item "-i"
Generate charts for all reports that support it. Normally, charts will
be generated only if the variable \fILR_INCLUDEIMAGES\fR is set to 1.
.IP "\fB\-o\fR \fIoutput format\fR" 4
.IX Item "-o output format"
One of \fBpdf\fR, \fBhtml\fR, \fBhtml_page\fR, \fBxhtml\fR, \fBxhtml_page\fR, \fBtxt\fR,
\&\fBdocbookx\fR, \fBrtf\fR and \fBxml\fR. Per default, simple txt output is
generated.
.IP \fB\-v\fR 4
.IX Item "-v"
Prints Lire\*(Aqs version and exits.
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBlr_rawmail2mail\fR can be used to automatically process reply from an
Online Responder which contains a XML report. It will extract the
report (which should have a content type of text/xml)
and deanonymized it. It will then use the \fBlr_xml2mail\fR\|(1) command to
formats and send the report to the recipients specified on the command
line.
.PP
The \fIdumpstem\fR argument is used by \fBlr_deanonymize\fR\|(1) to find the database
that was used in the anonymization process.
.PP
Environment variable TMPDIR, as set in sysconfdir/defaults, is used to
store tmpfiles; if LR_KEEP is set to a nonempty string, temporary files
are kept.
